+        // A rect laid over most of one widened view of a split screen: that view's own full-view effects (a fade to
+        // black, the flash of a hit), which the game draws over the view's viewport, a little inside its scissor, so they
+        // reach neither the pair's sides nor the view's. They are stretched with the view, or they stay in the 4:3
+        // middle of a view twice as wide as it is tall. Smaller rects (HUD panels) are left as they are. An untextured
+        // one (a fade, the death wipe's black) is drawn across the whole widened view: stretched alone it stopped a
+        // stretched inset short of the view's sides, a thin line of the scene at each.
+        auto coversSplitView = [&](const FixedRect &rect) -> const FixedRect * {
+            for (const FixedRect &view : wideViewScissors) {
